{
    "word": "betty",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e185be87-3df7-3bec-80a7-beda3c8f8e0b",
                "word": "Betty",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f947d339-0813-3810-a47b-81f42c779cd2",
                        "entry_id": "e185be87-3df7-3bec-80a7-beda3c8f8e0b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A diminutive of the female given name Elizabeth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f4f20dd-f63e-4278-bd64-59f8c2560a3a",
                                "sense_id": "f947d339-0813-3810-a47b-81f42c779cd2",
                                "text": "People in the last century weren't afraid of homely names; now we are all so smart and fine: no more \"Lady Bettys\" now."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e6fcac2-d719-4ae1-aefb-adbb7e2d71ee",
                                "sense_id": "f947d339-0813-3810-a47b-81f42c779cd2",
                                "text": "But Mrs. Betty Carver respects tradition, and this, I'm afraid, is ours. - - - She smells like expensive soap and her teeth are shiny-white. She does not in any way look like her name. It's not her fault that she was born in a time when people believed in names like Wanda, Dottie and Betty. She's more of a Vanessa or Paulina."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "64f000cf-7c44-4ebc-a0c9-7ac7ea9725e8",
                        "source_entry_id": "e185be87-3df7-3bec-80a7-beda3c8f8e0b",
                        "source_sense_id": "f947d339-0813-3810-a47b-81f42c779cd2",
                        "source_sense_description": "female name",
                        "target_lang_word": "Becia",
                        "target_lang_code": "pl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "4ceec065-890e-3c55-a43b-24f943bfa94f",
                "word": "betty",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3e7eb5a9-05da-488b-954a-3855fa2b4f32",
                        "entry_id": "4ceec065-890e-3c55-a43b-24f943bfa94f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "betties"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "40388582-9154-3ca0-9864-8aaad5326b1a",
                        "entry_id": "4ceec065-890e-3c55-a43b-24f943bfa94f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A short bar used by thieves to wrench doors open; a jimmy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b9cb2e8-b772-4779-97b2-b9f48d078b41",
                                "sense_id": "40388582-9154-3ca0-9864-8aaad5326b1a",
                                "text": "No modern Lycæum vvill ever equal thy Glory, […] deſcribing the povverful Betty, or the artful Picklock, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4beae701-b822-3739-b9b6-b72c5434106e",
                        "entry_id": "4ceec065-890e-3c55-a43b-24f943bfa94f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A picklock, skeleton key; a tool for opening locks."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "af5fe2fd-c637-4ddf-a0be-fb6f7e32185b",
                                "sense_id": "4beae701-b822-3739-b9b6-b72c5434106e",
                                "text": "After a quick meal at a tea shop, we found ourselves in the hallway at the Midland Hotel, where he removed a skeleton key, or “betty” as he called it, from his pocket and inserted it in the keyhole. […] Once they were out of sight, I fumbled about with the betty for a few moments before the lock finally clicked open."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "26ab2beb-32fb-3dc7-a492-fac8d920d886",
                        "entry_id": "4ceec065-890e-3c55-a43b-24f943bfa94f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A man who performs tasks that traditionally belong to a woman; (originally) an effeminate or gay man."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "derogatory"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f8c102ed-878f-3574-9d65-dae52431d97e",
                        "entry_id": "4ceec065-890e-3c55-a43b-24f943bfa94f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A pear-shaped bottle covered with straw, in which olive oil is sometimes brought from Italy; a Florence flask."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3161f221-0aa9-4476-911b-e3fb72309ece",
                                "sense_id": "f8c102ed-878f-3574-9d65-dae52431d97e",
                                "text": "On olive oil in casks, twenty cents per gallon; olive salad oil in bottles or betties, thirty per centum ad valorem"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bcaef27c-1fbc-3f75-96a4-f9a9a836b528",
                        "entry_id": "4ceec065-890e-3c55-a43b-24f943bfa94f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A baked dessert made with alternating layers of sweetened fruit and buttered bread crumbs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ceef1e38-41b5-43d4-a7fd-32c64dba274e",
                                "sense_id": "bcaef27c-1fbc-3f75-96a4-f9a9a836b528",
                                "text": "A pie-size betty is traditional, but if you like, assemble the recipe in individual ovenproof ramekins."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7ddfdd3f-066b-326b-b152-263c05317788",
                        "entry_id": "4ceec065-890e-3c55-a43b-24f943bfa94f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An attractive woman; a babe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "196015f2-ba79-4c3c-8566-bc0966767cbb",
                                "sense_id": "7ddfdd3f-066b-326b-b152-263c05317788",
                                "text": "Isn't my house classic? The columns date all the way back to 1972. Wasn't my Mom a betty? She died when I was just a baby. A fluke accident during a routine liposuction. I don't remember her, but I like to pretend she still watches over me."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
